4. _a-sza3 u3 e2_ i-na 
#tr.ts: eqlum u bītum ina
#tr.en: the field and the house, in

5. qa-ti la#-ma#-si2-ma 
#tr.ts: qāti lama(s)sīma
#tr.en: the hand of Lamassī alone

6. i-ba-asz-szi
#tr.ts: ibašši
#tr.en: will remain.

7. _ibila_ la-ma-si2 
#tr.ts: apil lama(s)sī
#tr.en: The heir of Lamassī

8. {disz}dingir-szu-i-bi-szu 
#tr.ts: ilšu-i(b)bīšu
#tr.en: is Ilšu-ibbīšu (and)

9. i-sza-x-szi u3 i-pa-qi2-si2 
#tr.ts: išalši (?) u ipa(q)qi(s)si
#tr.en: he will look after (?) her and provide her with food.
# x not AL (Stol), not KA (Klima), not LA (Schorr); CAD P, 125f reads AL

10. _mu_ {d}utu u3 su2-mu-la-el3 
#tr.ts: nīš šamaš u sumu-la-el
#tr.en: (By) the name of Šamaš and Sumu-la-el (they have sworn).

11. sza a-wa-at _dub_ 
#tr.ts: ša awat ṭuppim
#tr.en: Whoever the wording of this (from next line) tablet

12. an-ni-im u2-na-ka-ru 
#tr.ts: annîm una(k)karu
#tr.en: alters (is cursed).

13. _igi_ {d}utu-tab-ba-szu   
#tr.ts: maḫar šamaš-tappâšu
#tr.en: Before Šamaš-tappâšu;

14. _igi_ bur-nu-nu 
